(* expect:
nodeId is non-empty: true
nodeId carries a host suffix: true
nodeId is not the buildId: true
*)
(* rete#186: the node names its own BOARD. Sibling of 03_build_id.nsl beside it —
   buildId names the IMAGE, bootId names the RUN, this names the HARDWARE — and it
   exists because the third of those used to be a source constant. Whatever devkit
   was flashed with PortaBridgeNodeC6 wrote into the one `c6-bench` space: 36,153
   events across 19 distinct `obs/build` entries from at least two boards and two
   different apps, with nothing in the store able to say which. A porta space keyed
   on a slot cannot answer "what did THIS board do".

   Asserts SHAPE on host, because the host answer is `<hostname>-NNNN` — the machine
   plus four digits separating concurrent VMs on it (David, 2026-08-22). It therefore
   differs per machine and per process. On target the value is baked by
   zephyr/cmake/gen_node_id.cmake from the bench instance name, so it differs per board.
   Neither is pinnable; both have a checkable shape.

   The third line is the one worth having: `platform nodeId` and `platform buildId`
   are adjacent prims built by the same String idiom, and transposing the two cases
   in platform.c is a mistake that leaves both prims answering and every assertion
   about non-emptiness still passing. Comparing them catches it. *)
class NodeIdTest = () (
  public main: platform args: args = (
    | n b |
    n:: platform nodeId.
    b:: platform buildId.
    ('nodeId is non-empty: ', (n size > 0) printString) println.
    (* SHAPE, not value: a host VM answers `<host>-NNNN`, so the value differs per
       machine AND per process and pinning it would pin this bench into the suite.
       What is assertable is the shape the id promises — a '-' separating the host
       from four digits, with something on both sides. *)
    ('nodeId carries a host suffix: ',
       ((n size > 5) and: [ (n at: (n size - 4)) = 45 ]) printString) println.
    ('nodeId is not the buildId: ', (n = b) not printString) println.
    ^ 0 )
) : ()
